,\"sha256\":\"374004027c1e6c96150db00991a7879ee927add83ca6cf4f58f69728d7827b17\",\"size_bytes\":3700,\"source_id\":\"LOOM\",\"title\":\"Lot genealogy, patient linkage, privacy, and retention\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"110440234faec24dcf0f0e2e71c041f1d0a2ac22372b82a3fb35b6413fcc452c\",\"size_bytes\":4543,\"source_id\":\"MARCH\",\"title\":\"Facility notification, acknowledgment, and escalation\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"bad6b621c758f12c8ea10d44566d327a4e0ac844380263368a3aa9fe232c9e63\",\"size_bytes\":4248,\"source_id\":\"NORTH\",\"title\":\"Frozen recovery exercise defects and corrective evidence\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"07038e1bd8a752abec7bcd0b7aea965525f777dd5c06a06924491728fbc2f5b0\",\"size_bytes\":4270,\"source_id\":\"ONYX\",\"title\":\"Demand surge and supply-loss forecast revisions\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"0403c10933b14a017d20afebae2c044ce80e260b83c1116b7bd5b9da55826697\",\"size_bytes\":3971,\"source_id\":\"PIVOT\",\"title\":\"Independent readiness, falsification, and closure rules\"}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Exact current candidate\n{\"candidate_sha256\":\"a5adf105f06aa57e26868a4fae8422e2383ffba1bc57e50a72a077c3e534cac1\",\"candidate_version\":\"candidate-v000:a5adf105f06aa57e26868a4fae8422e2383ffba1bc57e50a72a077c3e534cac1\",\"files\":{\"BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md\":\"08548a5f6305764c54c031dfea7e7ae0b9367d242f16269fdf2d3427f5df2bc0\",\"EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md\":\"a1a4cc8b49d87602ed2ea51982569e6de92a0961ed8340f7381baf75af8ff291\"},\"schema\":\"architecture-current-candidate-v0\"}\n--- exact candidate file: EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md ---\n# Source Evidence Register\n\nSchema: source-slot-register-v0\nReadiness authority: none; exact sources and external evaluation govern.\n\n--- exact candidate file: BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md ---\n# Meridian Sterile-Infusion Recovery Decision\n\nCandidate not yet constructed.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"AXIOM\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"BRAMBLE\",\"start_line\":1}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:AXIOM:1-70+BRAMBLE:1-70\",\"object_version\":\"ff871ee116738e7a5fb554504292c6e60d76a6af51af846facf0405472cd8945\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"AXIOM\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"BRAMBLE\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8382}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"AXIOM\",\"source_path\":\"sources/AXIOM_AUTHORITY.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"968512cff889b2c6ebfd5c0e9a732ea29a12a9659fffbaa4ea010aba7cb4b775\",\"source_size_bytes\":4232,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Emergency manufacturing, recall, and release authority\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe independent quality unit places or releases a lot hold. The incident commander coordinates recovery, the regulator receives mandatory notice, and procurement executes an approved supplier choice; none may substitute for the quality release decision.\nA field recall begins on quality-unit recommendation and accountable-executive authorization. Emergency purchasing authority does not waive validated process, sterility, labeling, or traceability controls.\nA shift handoff is valid only when the receiving owner acknowledges the same recovery-candidate, affected-lot, and assay-plan versions. An unacknowledged handoff blocks closure.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nHazard evidence from BRAMBLE and HEATH informs the hold or release but does not itself create legal authority. Every manufacturing, allocation, and checker effect must bind one candidate version.\nA supplier or model-authored evidence slot is advisory work, never recall or release authority.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| AUTH-000 | quality-unit | r2 | 1.0 | approval | hold |\n| AUTH-001 | incident-commander | r2 | 1.7 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-002 | regulator | r2 | 2.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-003 | procurement | r2 | 3.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-004 | quality-unit | r2 | 3.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-005 | incident-commander | r2 | 1.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-006 | regulator | r2 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-007 | procurement | r2 | 2.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-008 | quality-unit | r2 | 3.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-009 | incident-commander | r2 | 1.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-010 | regulator | r2 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-011 | procurement | r2 | 2.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-012 | quality-unit | r2 | 3.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-013 | incident-commander | r2 | 3.9 | approval | hold |\n| AUTH-014 | regulator | r2 | 1.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-015 | procurement | r2 | 2.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-016 | quality-unit | r3 | 2.9 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-017 | incident-commander | r3 | 3.6 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-018 | regulator | r3 | 1.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-019 | procurement | r3 | 1.9 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-020 | quality-unit | r3 | 2.6 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-021 | incident-commander | r3 | 3.3 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-022 | regulator | r3 | 4.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-023 | procurement | r3 | 1.6 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-024 | quality-unit | r3 | 2.3 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-025 | incident-commander | r3 | 3.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-026 | regulator | r3 | 3.7 | approval | hold |\n| AUTH-027 | procurement | r3 | 1.3 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-028 | quality-unit | r3 | 2.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-029 | incident-commander | r3 | 2.7 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-030 | regulator | r3 | 3.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-031 | procurement | r3 | 1.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-032 | quality-unit | r4 | 1.7 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-033 | incident-commander | r4 | 2.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-034 | regulator | r4 | 3.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-035 | procurement | r4 | 3.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-036 | quality-unit | r4 | 1.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-037 | incident-commander | r4 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-038 | regulator | r4 | 2.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-039 | procurement | r4 | 3.5 | approval | hold |\n| AUTH-040 | quality-unit | r4 | 1.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-041 | incident-commander | r4 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-042 | regulator | r4 | 2.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-043 | procurement | r4 | 3.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-044 | quality-unit | r4 | 3.9 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-045 | incident-commander | r4 | 1.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-046 | regulator | r4 | 2.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-047 | procurement | r4 | 2.9 | approval | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nSeparate detection, recommendation, authorization, execution, verification, and closure.\nName the accountable owner and exact evidence needed to retire each hold.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"BRAMBLE\",\"source_path\":\"sources/BRAMBLE_CONTAMINATION.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"b5887292924f964689a1d92f2f9d7592183070bd5501148d5be30f58aa1619d4\",\"source_size_bytes\":3686,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Endotoxin, particulate, and assay-drift thresholds\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe alert threshold is 0.25 endotoxin units per milliliter and the rejection limit is 0.50 EU/mL. Values and units must not be converted into hours, percent, or temperature.\nTwo validated M41 samples measured 0.31 and 0.34 EU/mL. The lot remains held while the water-loop investigation is open even though neither value reaches the rejection limit.\nCurrent stability modeling assigns a 41 percent probability of assay drift after eighteen hours. That probability is not humidity, defect prevalence, or a readiness score.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nHEATH defines valid confirmation and release rounds; DRIFT and EMBER changes make prior line samples stale for the changed candidate.\nNORTH found that particulate inspection and endotoxin sampling were previously reported under mismatched lot revisions.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| QUAL-000 | lot-M41 | r2 | 0.2 | EU/mL | hold |\n| QUAL-001 | line-A | r2 | 0.9 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-002 | line-B | r2 | 1.6 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-003 | water-loop | r2 | 2.4 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-004 | lot-M41 | r2 | 3.0 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-005 | line-A | r2 | 0.7 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-006 | line-B | r2 | 1.4 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-007 | water-loop | r2 | 2.0 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-008 | lot-M41 | r2 | 2.8 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-009 | line-A | r2 | 0.3 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-010 | line-B | r2 | 1.1 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-011 | water-loop | r2 | 1.8 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-012 | lot-M41 | r2 | 2.5 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-013 | line-A | r2 | 3.1 | EU/mL | hold |\n| QUAL-014 | line-B | r2 | 0.8 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-015 | water-loop | r2 | 1.4 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-016 | lot-M41 | r3 | 2.1 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-017 | line-A | r3 | 2.9 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-018 | line-B | r3 | 0.5 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-019 | water-loop | r3 | 1.1 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-020 | lot-M41 | r3 | 1.9 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-021 | line-A | r3 | 2.5 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-022 | line-B | r3 | 3.2 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-023 | water-loop | r3 | 0.8 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-024 | lot-M41 | r3 | 1.6 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-025 | line-A | r3 | 2.2 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-026 | line-B | r3 | 3.0 | EU/mL | hold |\n| QUAL-027 | water-loop | r3 | 0.6 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-028 | lot-M41 | r3 | 1.2 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-029 | line-A | r3 | 1.9 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-030 | line-B | r3 | 2.6 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-031 | water-loop | r3 | 0.2 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-032 | lot-M41 | r4 | 0.9 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-033 | line-A | r4 | 1.6 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-034 | line-B | r4 | 2.4 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-035 | water-loop | r4 | 3.0 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-036 | lot-M41 | r4 | 0.7 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-037 | line-A | r4 | 1.4 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-038 | line-B | r4 | 2.0 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-039 | water-loop | r4 | 2.8 | EU/mL | hold |\n| QUAL-040 | lot-M41 | r4 | 0.3 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-041 | line-A | r4 | 1.1 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-042 | line-B | r4 | 1.8 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-043 | water-loop | r4 | 2.5 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-044 | lot-M41 | r4 | 3.1 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-045 | line-A | r4 | 0.8 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-046 | line-B | r4 | 1.4 | EU/mL | current |\n| QUAL-047 | water-loop | r4 | 2.1 | EU/mL | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve 0.25 EU/mL, 0.50 EU/mL, both observed results, and 41 percent with their exact meanings.\nState what starts, holds, expands, and retires the lot and line controls.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"DRIFT\",\"start_line\":1}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:CIPHER:1-70+DRIFT:1-70\",\"object_version\":\"44ca64381dab6ba11c59d9e1c94831e6478a3f84132f1c2f4ad7019b541cdb7a\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-002\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"DRIFT\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":9191}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"source_path\":\"sources/CIPHER_DEMAND.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"d625dbfdf7573704caf7a14a78e3601654e638074e8c94ab1317690f6df2e37f\",\"source_size_bytes\":4330,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Hospital demand, registry coverage, and overlapping critical cohorts\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe seventy-two-hour planning demand is 38,400 infusion bags: 18,200 adult acute-care, 7,600 pediatric, 6,900 dialysis, and 5,700 home-infusion allocations.\nThe registry covers 93 percent of recurring patients. The uncovered seven percent requires an uncertainty allowance; it is not a seven-percent demand reduction.\nPediatric, dialysis, immune-compromised, and home-infusion categories overlap. They cannot be added as independent people or independent bag demand without person-level reconciliation.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nGLINT sets clinical prioritization while FJORD and MARCH constrain verified delivery and acknowledgment. Supply must be compared with time-bound usable output after losses.\nA facility may hold local stock, but that stock counts only after lot, expiry, storage, and custody are verified through LOOM.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| DEM-000 | adult-ICU | r2 | 93.0 | percent-covered | hold |\n| DEM-001 | pediatric | r2 | 93.7 | percent-covered | current |\n| DEM-002 | dialysis | r2 | 94.4 | percent-covered | current |\n| DEM-003 | home-infusion | r2 | 95.1 | percent-covered | current |\n| DEM-004 | adult-ICU | r2 | 95.8 | percent-covered | current |\n| DEM-005 | pediatric | r2 | 93.4 | percent-covered | current |\n| DEM-006 | dialysis | r2 | 94.1 | percent-covered | current |\n| DEM-007 | home-infusion | r2 | 94.8 | percent-covered | current |\n| DEM-008 | adult-ICU | r2 | 95.5 | percent-covered | current |\n| DEM-009 | pediatric | r2 | 93.1 | percent-covered | current |\n| DEM-010 | dialysis | r2 | 93.8 | perce