| pediatric | r4 | 93.8 | percent-covered | current |\n| DEM-042 | dialysis | r4 | 94.5 | percent-covered | current |\n| DEM-043 | home-infusion | r4 | 95.2 | percent-covered | current |\n| DEM-044 | adult-ICU | r4 | 95.9 | percent-covered | current |\n| DEM-045 | pediatric | r4 | 93.5 | percent-covered | current |\n| DEM-046 | dialysis | r4 | 94.2 | percent-covered | current |\n| DEM-047 | home-infusion | r4 | 94.9 | percent-covered | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nState time horizon, population basis, overlap rule, registry uncertainty, and shortage allocation.\nDo not translate coverage into readiness or subtract uncovered demand.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"DRIFT\",\"source_path\":\"sources/DRIFT_CAPACITY.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"f1b10a1300f8f42742f6b3e17b8c3eb28020ce93b5ef8e382d1dc015858cfc6b\",\"source_size_bytes\":4407,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Fill-line output and shared sterilizer constraint\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nLine A is nominally rated for 14,000 bags per day and Line B for 11,000, but both depend on Sterilizer 3, whose validated sustainable limit is 18,000 bags per day. The line ratings cannot be summed to claim 25,000.\nThe last integrated run produced 16,200 released bags per day after inspection loss and changeover. Higher output requires a current candidate-bound line, sterilizer, inspection, and laboratory check.\nLine B cannot use alternate caps without EMBER dimensional qualification and a new container-closure integrity sample plan.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nIRIS power and JASPER staffing may reduce usable capacity below validated output. KNOLL alternate production shares the same inspection-cell contractor.\nAny line, sterilizer cycle, component, or shift mutation makes prior throughput and release evidence stale.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| CAP-000 | line-A | r2 | 16.2 | thousand-bags/day | hold |\n| CAP-001 | line-B | r2 | 16.9 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-002 | sterilizer-3 | r2 | 17.6 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-003 | inspection-cell | r2 | 18.3 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-004 | line-A | r2 | 19.0 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-005 | line-B | r2 | 16.6 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-006 | sterilizer-3 | r2 | 17.3 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-007 | inspection-cell | r2 | 18.0 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-008 | line-A | r2 | 18.7 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-009 | line-B | r2 | 16.3 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-010 | sterilizer-3 | r2 | 17.0 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-011 | inspection-cell | r2 | 17.7 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-012 | line-A | r2 | 18.4 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-013 | line-B | r2 | 19.1 | thousand-bags/day | hold |\n| CAP-014 | sterilizer-3 | r2 | 16.7 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-015 | inspection-cell | r2 | 17.4 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-016 | line-A | r3 | 18.1 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-017 | line-B | r3 | 18.8 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-018 | sterilizer-3 | r3 | 16.4 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-019 | inspection-cell | r3 | 17.1 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-020 | line-A | r3 | 17.8 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-021 | line-B | r3 | 18.5 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-022 | sterilizer-3 | r3 | 19.2 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-023 | inspection-cell | r3 | 16.8 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-024 | line-A | r3 | 17.5 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-025 | line-B | r3 | 18.2 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-026 | sterilizer-3 | r3 | 18.9 | thousand-bags/day | hold |\n| CAP-027 | inspection-cell | r3 | 16.5 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-028 | line-A | r3 | 17.2 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-029 | line-B | r3 | 17.9 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-030 | sterilizer-3 | r3 | 18.6 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-031 | inspection-cell | r3 | 16.2 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-032 | line-A | r4 | 16.9 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-033 | line-B | r4 | 17.6 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-034 | sterilizer-3 | r4 | 18.3 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-035 | inspection-cell | r4 | 19.0 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-036 | line-A | r4 | 16.6 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-037 | line-B | r4 | 17.3 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-038 | sterilizer-3 | r4 | 18.0 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-039 | inspection-cell | r4 | 18.7 | thousand-bags/day | hold |\n| CAP-040 | line-A | r4 | 16.3 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-041 | line-B | r4 | 17.0 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-042 | sterilizer-3 | r4 | 17.7 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-043 | inspection-cell | r4 | 18.4 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-044 | line-A | r4 | 19.1 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-045 | line-B | r4 | 16.7 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-046 | sterilizer-3 | r4 | 17.4 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n| CAP-047 | inspection-cell | r4 | 18.1 | thousand-bags/day | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nUse the shared 18,000 limit and observed 16,200 output until current testing proves more.\nBind equipment, component, inspection loss, staffing, power, and release effects.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","generated":""}
