1 | percent-yield | current |\n| COMP-041 | bag-film | r4 | 88.8 | percent-yield | current |\n| COMP-042 | port-set | r4 | 89.5 | percent-yield | current |\n| COMP-043 | label-stock | r4 | 90.2 | percent-yield | current |\n| COMP-044 | cap-17 | r4 | 90.9 | percent-yield | current |\n| COMP-045 | bag-film | r4 | 88.5 | percent-yield | current |\n| COMP-046 | port-set | r4 | 89.2 | percent-yield | current |\n| COMP-047 | label-stock | r4 | 89.9 | percent-yield | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nDistinguish target lead time from observed arrival and component yield from demand.\nDo not release alternate components on catalog equivalence alone.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"FJORD\",\"source_path\":\"sources/FJORD_DISTRIBUTION.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"de932f76c00ed9529577cfcb20eb79afd44b847ea9c4e543533d0d7d856dd9be\",\"source_size_bytes\":4054,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Cold-chain distribution, routes, and custody\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nReleased bags must remain between 2 and 8 degrees Celsius. A single value of 2.8 degrees is not a valid replacement for that range.\nThe river route shortens travel by forty minutes but has a six-hour bridge-closure risk. The north route is ninety minutes longer and has current generator-backed cross-dock capacity.\nA temperature excursion starts a hold at the affected pallet and lot level. Delivery completion requires logger review, custody handoff, and facility acknowledgment.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nCIPHER allocation, GLINT clinical priority, IRIS backup power, LOOM lot identity, and MARCH acknowledgment form one delivery claim.\nChanging route, cross-dock, pallet, logger, or receiving facility makes prior distribution verification inapplicable to the changed movement.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| COLD-000 | north-route | r2 | 5.1 | degrees-C | hold |\n| COLD-001 | river-route | r2 | 5.8 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-002 | cross-dock | r2 | 6.5 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-003 | hospital-dock | r2 | 7.2 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-004 | north-route | r2 | 7.9 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-005 | river-route | r2 | 5.5 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-006 | cross-dock | r2 | 6.2 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-007 | hospital-dock | r2 | 6.9 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-008 | north-route | r2 | 7.6 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-009 | river-route | r2 | 5.2 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-010 | cross-dock | r2 | 5.9 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-011 | hospital-dock | r2 | 6.6 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-012 | north-route | r2 | 7.3 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-013 | river-route | r2 | 8.0 | degrees-C | hold |\n| COLD-014 | cross-dock | r2 | 5.6 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-015 | hospital-dock | r2 | 6.3 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-016 | north-route | r3 | 7.0 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-017 | river-route | r3 | 7.7 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-018 | cross-dock | r3 | 5.3 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-019 | hospital-dock | r3 | 6.0 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-020 | north-route | r3 | 6.7 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-021 | river-route | r3 | 7.4 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-022 | cross-dock | r3 | 8.1 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-023 | hospital-dock | r3 | 5.7 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-024 | north-route | r3 | 6.4 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-025 | river-route | r3 | 7.1 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-026 | cross-dock | r3 | 7.8 | degrees-C | hold |\n| COLD-027 | hospital-dock | r3 | 5.4 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-028 | north-route | r3 | 6.1 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-029 | river-route | r3 | 6.8 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-030 | cross-dock | r3 | 7.5 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-031 | hospital-dock | r3 | 5.1 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-032 | north-route | r4 | 5.8 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-033 | river-route | r4 | 6.5 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-034 | cross-dock | r4 | 7.2 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-035 | hospital-dock | r4 | 7.9 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-036 | north-route | r4 | 5.5 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-037 | river-route | r4 | 6.2 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-038 | cross-dock | r4 | 6.9 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-039 | hospital-dock | r4 | 7.6 | degrees-C | hold |\n| COLD-040 | north-route | r4 | 5.2 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-041 | river-route | r4 | 5.9 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-042 | cross-dock | r4 | 6.6 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-043 | hospital-dock | r4 | 7.3 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-044 | north-route | r4 | 8.0 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-045 | river-route | r4 | 5.6 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-046 | cross-dock | r4 | 6.3 | degrees-C | current |\n| COLD-047 | hospital-dock | r4 | 7.0 | degrees-C | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nState temperature range, route, delay, power, custody, excursion response, and acknowledgment.\nDo not equate dispatch, arrival, or one logger reading with usable clinical delivery.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","generated":""}
